---
import BioPage from '../../components/BioPage.astro';

// Wording is carried over from the live page. Changes from the live page, for Bryn's review:
//  - Title is "Firm Administrator" (owner's decision, 10-28-26: she is not presented as a paralegal); the live page said "Certified Paralegal".
//    The meta description drops "certified" for the same reason.
//  - The live sidebar listed "Current - Juris Doctor", but the biography says she graduated in 2024.
//    The sidebar now matches the biography. Bryn to confirm.
//  - The live page listed three items under "Awards" that are really two associations and one honor;
//    they are sorted into "Honor" and "Associations".
//  - Pre-launch review R-10 (owner approved, 10-30-26): one plain sentence on bar status follows the law school
//    paragraph. She is not an attorney; do not call her one anywhere.
const title = 'Mandy Truman - Pathfinder Injury Law';
const description =
  'Pathfinder Injury Law is a family business, and Mandy Truman serves as firm administrator. Read more about her journey.';
const facts = [
  {
    heading: 'Education',
    items: [
      'Juris Doctor, University of Richmond School of Law (Summa Cum Laude, 2024)',
      'Bachelor of Science, University of Richmond (Summa Cum Laude, 2021)',
      'Associate of Applied Science in Paralegal Studies, J. Sargeant Reynolds (Magna Cum Laude)',
    ],
  },
  { heading: 'Honor', items: ['Virginia Lawyers Weekly Unsung Legal Hero'] },
  {
    heading: 'Associations',
    items: ['Virginia Paralegal Association', 'National Association of Legal Assistants'],
  },
];
---
<BioPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/mandy-truman/"
  name="Mandy Truman"
  role="Firm Administrator"
  photo="/images/photos/mandy.jpg"
  photoAlt="Mandy Truman, firm administrator at Pathfinder Injury Law"
  facts={facts}
>
  <p class="lead">
    Pathfinder is a family business, and Mandy Truman rounds out the Pathfinder team as firm
    administrator.
  </p>

  <h2 id="about">About Mandy Truman</h2>
  <p>
    Mandy Truman is Pathfinder’s firm administrator, the strategic brains behind the operation, and is married to Bryn. Mandy brings years of workers’ compensation experience to her
    work with Pathfinder. She was born and raised in Mechanicsville, Virginia. Her career in workers’
    compensation began as a teenager with a position at the Virginia Workers’ Compensation
    Commission. She later worked at the Supreme Court of Virginia and as a paralegal at a workers’
    compensation defense firm in Richmond. This gave way to forming Pathfinder Injury Law with Bryn
    while the two sat in their hospital room the day their son was born in August 2019.
  </p>
  <p>
    Given her experience in the various levels of the judicial system and her work as a defense
    paralegal, Mandy brings invaluable perspective on the inner workings of insurance companies and
    the judiciary. She has a strong interest in legal research and writing and can often be found at
    her desk with empty coffee cups, snack containers, Legos, and law books strewn about, notes and
    flags sticking out everywhere and questionable 80s music playing (to Bryn’s dismay).
  </p>
  <p>
    Mandy earned her Bachelor of Science summa cum laude in 2021 from the University of Richmond. She
    then attended the University of Richmond School of Law, from which she graduated in 2024 summa
    cum laude, in the top five students in her class. She received no less than six CALI awards for
    scoring the highest grades in various classes; was on Law Review; and was inducted into the Order
    of the Coif. She further served as President of the Animal Law Society, Vice President of First
    Generation Law Students, and Networking and Alumni Relations Chair for the Phi Alpha Delta law
    fraternity. This, while also raising a small child and helping run a law firm.
    Mandy will be licensed to practice law once she passes the Virginia bar exam.
  </p>
  <p>
    In her free time, Mandy enjoys reading, listening to music, hanging out with the family and the
    hounds, and drinking way too much coffee.
  </p>
</BioPage>
